{
  "dom_id": "step-q182615",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Find the missing values in the following truth table:\n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,Q∨¬(P∨Q)\\,$ | $\\,¬P∨Q\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-1}} | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-2}} | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-3}} |\n\nUsing your results, complete the following statement:\n\n$$\nQ∨¬(P∨Q){{field-4}}¬P∨Q\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "First, let's solve for the missing values:\n\n- When $P≡\\text{T}$ and $Q≡\\text{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q∨¬(P∨Q) & ≡\\text{T}∨¬(\\text{T}∨\\text{T}) \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}∨¬\\text{T} \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}∨\\text{F} \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $P≡\\text{T}$ and $Q≡\\text{F},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q∨¬(P∨Q) & ≡\\text{F}∨¬(\\text{T}∨\\text{F}) \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}∨¬\\text{T} \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}∨\\text{F} \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $P≡\\text{F}$ and $Q≡\\text{F},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬P∨Q & ≡¬\\text{F}∨\\text{F} \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}∨\\text{F} \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur completed table is shown below. \n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,Q∨¬(P∨Q)\\,$ | $\\,¬P∨Q\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nTo determine whether $Q∨¬(P∨Q)$ is logically equivalent to $¬P∨Q,$ we need to check whether their truth tables are equivalent.\n\nLooking at the last two columns, we see that they are the same $(\\text{T},\\text{F},\\text{T},\\text{T}).$ Therefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\nQ∨¬(P∨Q)≡¬P∨Q.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
